    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0285" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg205"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-06-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 599.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 526 of
                    January 7, and to my dispatch No. 503 of February 8 last, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith a copy of a note from the Marquis of Lansdowne, suggesting <pb
                        facs="0286" n="206" xml:id="pg206"/> that the Government of the Kongo Free
                    State be notified that Mr. Casement, His Britannic Majesty’s consul, has been
                    authorized to take charge of American interests there.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d191-a1.xml" xpointer="d191-a1"/>
            </div>
